This document gives an English description of what has changed in the
most recent version of the Linux FAQ.

Comments on and submissions for the FAQ are strongly encouraged and
welcomed - I don't have time to read every article in col.help, and
thus need your assistance to spot the FAQ-threads that I miss.


Changes November - December 1994.

New Questions:
Q4.10. My root filesystem is read-only !
Q12.3. I want to mail someone about my problem.

Modified Questions:
Q2.9.  Are the newsgroups archived      Added Web-accessible archive.
Q3.5.  Can I access BSD FFS, ...        xhfs0.3 (for Macintosh) added.
Q7.3.  How do I set the timezone ?      Make sure kernel time is correct GMT.
Q7.11. ... more than 128Mb of swap ?    Was 16Mb, and moved from `obsolete'.
Q10.2. Where can I get an XF86Config    Missed a Xconfig -> XF86config change.


Changes October - November 1994.

New Questions:
Q5.10.  Does Linux support threads or lightweight processes ?

Modified Questions:
Q1.2.  What software does it support ?  Where to get iBCS2 info.
Q1.4.  What ports to other processors   68K and PowerPC info updated.
Q3.5.  Can I access BSD FFS, ...        Amiga FFS patch location.
Q8.1.  What is a .gz file ? ...         gunzip is a link to gzip
Q8.6.  How should I pronounce Linux ?   Added "Leenooks" parody.
Q10.2. Where can I get an XF86Config    It's not an Xconfig any more.
Q10.3. xterm logins show up strangely   still in XF86 2.1, fixed in 3.1


All question numbers should refer to the numbering in the new edition
in each case (eg, for the January to February changes the numbers
would refer to the February edition).

