(From the README file)

Xm++/CommonInteract    User Interface Development System
===================

Xm++ is a user interface framework for the C++ language. It is
designed to be a simple and intuitive programming interface to
access the functionality of commonly used GUI toolkit objects.
The first release was completely built upon X11 and the X Toolkit.
Over the time Xm++ turned into an experimental system for developing
multi platform and client/server GUIs.

Today the implementation supports Motif, Xaw (to a limited extent)
and TIP/RCI - the Toolkit Interface Protocol, a c/s GUI which
allows Xm++ applications to run over a network and/or on non-UNIX
systems. (See the release notes for more info on TIP.)


(From the README.0.62 file)

