The NAGWare f90 Compiler, version 2.1, is now available
for Linux.  Version 2.1 is the latest release of the world's
first Fortran 90 compiler, originally introduced in 1991, and
it is now the first Fortran 90 compiler to be ported to Linux.

Version 2.1 remains the most robust compiler on the market for
any platform.  It now features optional run-time garbage collection
with user control; FORALL statement and construct; nested FORALL
and WHERE constructs; all of the new High Performance Fortran
(HPF) language features and intrinsic functions (single processor
target); performance improvements, particularly in SPREAD, RESHAPE
and MATMUL; improved support of IEEE arithmetic exception
handling; automatic file pre-connection; and more common
FORTRAN 77 extensions may be used including Hollerith constants.

