CORRECTION

In our original announcement of Slackware Professional Linux 2.1, we made
a few naming errors regarding XFree86 3.1. The good folks over at XFree86.Org
pointed these out to us and asked us to correct our posting as well as
our Web server. This has been done. An updated copy of the product
announcement can be found on http://www.morse.net.

Please note the following changes/corrections to our original posting:

The "SOFTWARE HIGHLIGHTS" section should be modified as shown here:
	. Includes a complete distribution of XFree86-3.1 (X11R6 based)
	. All binaries have been recompiled to take advantage of
	  the new XFree86 libraries.

The "MAJOR ENHANCEMENTS SINCE 2.0" section should be modified as shown
here:
	XFree86-3.1 (X11R6 based) is now the default windowing system.
	All X binaries have been recompiled to use the new XFree86
	shared libraries. XFree86 offers added support for many new
	video chipsets and extends the reliability of support for
	others.

