Subject: Patch to ppp-2.1.2b.tar.gz for dev_kfree_skb
Followup-To: comp.os.linux.misc
Date: 13 Dec 1994 18:15:13 +0200
Organization: ?
Lines: 37
Sender: wirzeniu@cc.Helsinki.FI
Approved: linux-announce@tc.cornell.edu (Lars Wirzenius)
Message-ID: <3ckhah$iem@kruuna.Helsinki.FI>
NNTP-Posting-Host: kruuna.helsinki.fi
Mime-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=ISO-8859-1
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit
Keywords: ppp, net-2-debugged, patch
Description: Patch to the ppp-2.1.2b.tar.gz file for the 1.0 series kernels

The file ppp-2.1.2b.tar.gz file is on sunsite and its mirrors. It is
the PPP support for Linux and other systems.

I have found a problem with the ppp-2.1.2b.tar.gz file and building
kernels for the 1.0 series (with Net-2-Debugged.)

Apparently, I used the new name for a function without allowing the
old name to be used for Net-2-Debugged.

If you compiled the kernel with the 'un-patched' code you will find that
it will reference a procedure called 'dev_kfree_skb'. This is the new
name for the Net-2-Debugged routing 'kfree_skb'.

This patch corrects the file. Sorry for any difficulties which this may
have caused people.

--- drivers/net/ppp.c.orig	Tue Dec  6 06:36:19 1994
+++ drivers/net/ppp.c	Tue Dec  6 06:36:54 1994
@@ -66,8 +66,9 @@
 #include <dev.h>
 #include <skbuff.h>
 #include <inet.h>
 #define	skb_queue_head_init(buf)	*(buf) = NULL
+#define	dev_kfree_skb			kfree_skb
 #else					/* v1.1.5 and later */
 #include <linux/netdevice.h>
 #include <linux/skbuff.h>
 #include <linux/inet.h>

-- 
Al Longyear           longyear@netcom.com



